// "Blocking" = the fully directional block fact, BOTH sides narrowed at
// once ([CR#509.1g..509.1h]) — "<subject> blocks <object>"
// ([CR#509.3b]: "Whenever [a creature] blocks a creature, …") and its
// passive-voice mirror "<object> becomes blocked by <subject>"
// ([CR#509.3d]: "Whenever [a creature] becomes blocked by a creature, …").
// event/Blocks + event/BecomesBlocked only narrow ONE side (the other
// defaults to any); this narrows both. Told apart on the render side by
// which slot is `Ref(This)`. Mirrors event/DealsCombatDamage's two-param
// shape. Usage: Blocking(by, of) — e.g. Blocking(Ref(This), Creature) for
// "~ blocks a creature", Blocking(Creature, Ref(This)) for "~ becomes
// blocked by a creature".
(
    name: "Blocking",
    template: "${0} blocks ${1}",
    kinds: [EventFilter],
    params: [Predicate, Predicate],
    body: BlockDeclared(by: Param(0), of: Param(1)),
)
